package ReviewCenter {
    part def ThreadService {
        doc /* Starts comment threads on a file of a review or on a check of its frozen checklist, appends replies, resolves and reopens threads, enforces the comment rules (a comment on the lines of a file only when they exist on the chosen side: the head, or the baseline for a file that has one; a thread carries its side), records the signed-in user as the author, and reads threads back. A thread is a Question (chat, the default) or a Finding (`ThreadKind`); every comment is a Comment or a Resolution (`ReviewCommentKind`) and carries `IncludeInReport` (default false). Only the included comments of the thread are part of the record digest, so chat never makes a signature out of date. The service promotes a Question to a Finding and demotes it back (`PromoteAsync`, `DemoteAsync`), toggles the inclusion of a comment (`SetCommentReportAsync`), and resolves a thread (a Finding needs a resolution note, which is stored as a Resolution comment in the same transaction; the store compares the kind it reads in that transaction with the kind the service saw and refuses a changed kind with the RecordChanged rule, and a resolved thread can only be reached through that resolve, since the only other state change is a reopen); the permissions come from the pure helper `ThreadKindRules` and the role names from `ReviewActorRoles`, an Auditor can never promote or demote, and every such change is audited. Every change by an actor requires that the actor may see the project (`IProjectAccess`) and that the review is not concluded (ReviewLocked, `ReviewLock.IsConcluded`), and refuses a change that would alter the digest and so make a current signature out of date unless the caller acknowledges the affected slots (SignaturesWouldBecomeOutOfDate). Also derives what a reader needs to navigate the discussion: a thread's last activity, the thread index (rows across all files, filtered by state and ordered by activity), and the one-sentence next step, which also names the unanswered checklist checks and the checks answered Fail. It also tells a viewer which actions are allowed (`GetCapabilitiesAsync`: per thread whether it may be promoted, demoted or resolved and which replies may be added to or removed from the report, by the same rules that the actions enforce; nothing for an Auditor, an API token or a concluded review), and `ThreadCounts` counts the threads by kind and state for the summary strip, the progress and the inbox. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.ReviewCenter.Core/ThreadService.cs, ThreadCounts.cs, ThreadCapabilities.cs, ThreadKindRules.cs, ThreadKind.cs, ReviewCommentKind.cs, ReviewActorRoles.cs, ReviewThread.cs, ThreadAnchor.cs, CheckThreadRules.cs, ReviewComment.cs, ReviewThreadState.cs, and FileText.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.ReviewCenter.Tests/Core/ThreadServiceTests.cs, ThreadServiceReportTests.cs, ThreadCapabilitiesTests.cs, ThreadKindRulesTests.cs, CheckThreadTests.cs, and CheckThreadRulesTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/review-center/core/thread-service.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/review-center/core/thread-service.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/review-center/core/thread-service.yaml */
    }
}
